{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1221890-plans-and-schemes-of-lower-power-npcs","id":1221890,"title":"Plans and Schemes of Lower Power NPCs","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-05-24T17:37:18-07:00","id":1221890,"title":"Plans and Schemes of Lower Power NPCs","content":"Hi there. I am currently running a game of Mage: the Awakening. The setting I am running has a lot of wizards and not very much mana.<br /> <br /> Usually when I am running a game, I think of the mistakes players have made in previous games. Of not fully thought through plans that have pitfalls built into them. I make the lower powered NPCs do these things. They can make for amusing side plots and make the PCs feel smart and clever as they foil these plots on their way toward the bigger conflicts in the setting. <br /> <br /> Anyway, I am asking for STs and Players to give me examples of what hairbrained schemes and mistakes have PCs or NPCs made in your games? <br /> <br /> I am looking forward to hearing about your games. Thanks! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There Are Four Lights!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/92949-baltimore-the-kiddie-pool-saga-pics-maps-and-links\" target=\"_blank\">[Actual Play] Baltimore: The Kiddie Pool Saga</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead","name":"figurehead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar64_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T18:31:39-07:00","id":1221899,"title":"","content":"My players were supposed to investigate a local drug ring with supernatural connections. This was by order of the Sentinel and was supposed to be a nice intro to the local Mage scene. 1 of my players A death obsessed Thyrsus anthropologist asked ghosts and spirits about the place and got some solid information my other players a forces street justice obrimos and two matter loving Moros decided to use matter to turn the water in the sprinklers in the warehouse into kerosine and the use forces to make the power surge high enough to pop the light bulbs and then turn the electricity into fire killing the 12 thugs inside and royally pissing off their sin eater boss leading to what was the first of many times that a cabal member almost died. Or the time the Thrysus took a shitload of LSD and went into the underworld, or the time the Obrimos went to beat the shit out of the Asshole Mastigos NPC who was a high ranking member of the Sliver Ladder and horrifyingly enough succeeded, or the time that the Guardian of the Veil Moros (yes one of the two from earlier) proceeded to kidnap another NPC bring him down into the underworld and give him over to his dead ancestor to possess. these are all things my players did while lower than Gnosis 4... hope this helps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24168,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24168-madman777","user":"Madman777","date":". 05-24-2018, 09:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24168-madman777","name":"Madman777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-25T11:45:07-07:00","id":1222098,"title":"","content":"Stuff I have personally done: used a massive amount to mind magic and my allies in the police force to form what amounted to a drug cartel in a small Midwestern town. Became Mayor of said town. Regularly harvested the Goetia which he then sent back out to cause more addicts to perpetuate a horrible cycle. Needless to say he was a very low wisdom character with resources 5 and a ton of shady allies/contacts eventually I received a paradox worth 6 successes and was brutally destroyed by a gulmoth. It was the first time the ST had been happy to kill a pc. My next character was a adamantine arrow acanthus who was the epitome of the phrase the road to hell is paved with good intentions. I was trying to get into the dioane legacy and basically ended up cursing/blessing a ton of people one of whom turned out to be a cop possessed by the Lord of Irons Strix from requiem. The Strix went on a massive killing spree (I fate triggered it to last until he willing left the police for or retired and then released it because I'm an idiot) so he got 8 again on all brawl weaponry and firearms rolls (but I am a powerful idiot) which he then used to wipe out any who opposed him. Including but not limited the 2 pc sleepwalkers in our group who knowing what he was and what blessing he had from me both in and out of character decided to bum rush him... They died in 4 rounds after one got used as a human shield and died from the other shooting through him and then after sleepwalker 2 had run out of ammo the lord of irons threw the now dead sleepwalker 1 on top of her pinning her under him and inflicting the knockdown tilt calmly walked over and shot her in the head. Killing her ( 8 again and a heavy pistol + 8 dice = dead idiot) and then using their smartphones to track down our sanctum where the ensuing fight took 2 hours, killed our Thyrsus(paradox from healing spells + bullets) and left me and our Moros near death as in all lethal except one box for him and and 4 aggravated 5 lethal one box clear for me. To kill him not knowing he could jump bodies. Which he did. We died the next night because while my blessing was gone he had the entire police force on his side and we hadn't really had a chance to heal yet. Fun Times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24168-madman777","name":"Madman777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-27T14:22:04-07:00","id":1222508,"title":"","content":"Thanks Madman for posting! I will be using a few of these in tomorrow's game. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There Are Four Lights!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/92949-baltimore-the-kiddie-pool-saga-pics-maps-and-links\" target=\"_blank\">[Actual Play] Baltimore: The Kiddie Pool Saga</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead","name":"figurehead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar64_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-27T14:51:34-07:00","id":1222520,"title":"","content":"Happy to help! Let me know how it goes. Also if you want anymore stories I have a ton of them both hysterical, and really really stupid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24168-madman777","name":"Madman777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-04T14:09:50-07:00","id":1224804,"title":"","content":"I once had a group that encountered a Ban against the Awakened which they traversed by temporarily masking their Auras. They got into a fight and the Acanthus in the group decided to cast Acceleration and high tail it at maximum speed right into the Ban, which he forgot was there. I was kind enough to just inflict 5 bashing (his speed multiple) on him for forgetting. It did later result in him losing consciousness earlier than he might have during the ensuing battle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-24T15:44:29-07:00","id":1229869,"title":"","content":"How about grasping further than they can handle ? Low power does not mean low ambition or intelligence. For example, lets say an NPC cabal learns about 3 things:<br /> <br /> 1- An imbued item the Lex Magicka confiscated from a Reaper, which he used to extract and store minds and souls for later consumption.<br /> <br /> 2- An artifact the Mysterium used to bind spirits to an area for research experiments.<br /> <br /> 3- An old diary, which leads to the workshop of an Adamantine Arrow faction that wanted to make an army of golem supersoldiers. One day they suddenly vanished without a trace.<br /> <br /> So now they want to gather these items, create a super body, transfer one of them into it and bind a high Ranking spirit inside it, wielding its powers and going &quot;A god am I&quot;, becoming stronger than most masters. Of course, they would be playing with an item utterly tainted by a Reaper's Nimbus (not to mention any other mojo he worked on it), have a monomaniacal magical entity for a roommate and be in a body created with tools made by mages, on which they have next to no information. All that can backfire terribly, and proceed quietly in the background. No mage worth his salt would make those mistakes, but they are inexperienced and full of Hubris, power can tempt even the most meticulous mind to get sloppy, all it takes is for one member to be impulsive. And the consequences of that, either backfiring or succeeding, can make for good plot hooks. Imbued items are fun, they can let clever planners wield power they have no business having and bend the rules in interesting ways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 06-24-2018, 09:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}